UID:padimai-onchain-artist-residency-oops-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: Padimai: OOPS Onchain Artist Residency 2026
DESCRIPTION:OOPS (Origin Of Primary Source) is the first edition of Padimai
  Art and Tech Studio's Onchain Artist Residency\, a three-month remote res
 idency inviting art practitioners to critically and creatively engage with
  NFTs as artistic registers and as systems of knowledge\, documentation\, 
 and access. Five practitioners are selected. SUPPORT: SGD 15\,000 honorari
 um per artist\, plus SGD 5\,000 per artist for documentation. The residenc
 y is remote\, with community engagement designed through online meetings\;
  at the end\, participants deliver three NFTs developed during the residen
 cy to Padimai. ELIGIBILITY: individual creative practitioners working at t
 he intersection of art\, technology\, and blockchain\; open internationall
 y. RESIDENCY: 20 September to 20 December 2026. DEADLINE: 15 August 2026. 
 Apply via the residency page.\n\nOrganisation: Padimai Art and Tech Studio
 \nLocation: Remote residency (Padimai is based in Singapore)\; open intern
 ationally.\nAward: SGD 15\,000 honorarium per artist plus an additional SG
 D 5\,000 per artist for documentation (audio\, video\, photography). Five 
 practitioners selected. No application fee.\nDuration: 3 months (20 Septem
 ber to 20 December 2026)\n\nMore: https://padimai.net/onchain-artist-resid
 ency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://padimai.net/onchain-artist-residency/?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote residency (Padimai is based in Singapore)\; open internatio
 nally.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:al-purdy-aframe-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260918
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260919
SUMMARY:Deadline: Al Purdy A-frame Association: Al and Eurithe Purdy Reside
 ncy 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Al Purdy A-frame Residency offers Canadian writers time and
  space to work at the historic A-frame home built by poet Al Purdy and his
  wife Eurithe on Roblin Lake in Ameliasburgh\, Prince Edward County\, Onta
 rio. Poetry is prioritized\, but all writers are welcome. SUPPORT: CAD 750
  per week stipend and paid return travel (subject to the Association's fun
 draising and Canada Council matching)\; residencies run 3 to 12 weeks. ELI
 GIBILITY: Canadian citizens or permanent residents only. DEADLINE: 18 Sept
 ember 2026 (postmark\, or 4:00pm PT for electronic submissions). Apply via
  the residency page.\n\nOrganisation: The Al Purdy A-frame Association\nLo
 cation: Ameliasburgh\, Prince Edward County\, Ontario\, Canada. Canadian c
 itizens or permanent residents only.\nAward: CAD 750 per week stipend plus
  paid return travel to Ameliasburgh (funding subject to the Association's 
 fundraising and Canada Council matching). Terms of 3 to 12 weeks. No appli
 cation fee.\nDuration: 3 to 12 weeks\n\nMore: https://www.alpurdy.ca/resid
 ency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.alpurdy.ca/residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Ameliasburgh\, Prince Edward County\, Ontario\, Canada. Canadian c
 itizens or permanent residents only.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:atheras-nicosia-ludic-lab-toyful-music-festival-2026@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260715
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260716
SUMMARY:Deadline: Atheras: Nicosia Ludic Lab for Composers\, Toyful Music F
 estival 2026
DESCRIPTION:Atheras Peoples and Cultures invites composers and performer-re
 searchers to apply for the Nicosia Ludic Lab\, a 31-day international resi
 dency dedicated to exploring 'play' as a compositional and performative me
 thodology in contemporary music. Building on the artistic vision of the To
 yful Music Festival\, the residency creates a focused environment where ex
 perimentation\, precision\, and imagination coexist\, redefining how music
  is conceived\, structured\, and performed. The residency runs in Nicosia\
 , Cyprus\, from 23 October to 22 November 2026\, and participants develop 
 new ensemble works that directly shape the artistic programme of the Toyfu
 l Music Festival 2026. ELIGIBILITY: applications are open to individual ar
 tists (proposals from duets or collectives will not be considered) based i
 n a Creative Europe country\, who must demonstrate a strong interest in ex
 perimental\, ensemble-based practices. SELECTED RESIDENTS RECEIVE: full fi
 nancial support (travel\, accommodation\, daily allowance)\; shared accomm
 odation in central Nicosia\; continuous access to a professional ensemble\
 ; mentorship sessions and individual meetings with ensemble members\; coac
 hing sessions with composer and conductor Andys Skordis\; artistic and pro
 fessional guidance from the Atheras team\; rehearsal space and full produc
 tion support for Phase 3\; and video and audio recording of the final live
  concert for documentation and international visibility. Deadline: 15 July
  2026.\n\nOrganisation: Atheras Peoples and Cultures\nLocation: Nicosia\, 
 Cyprus\; open to individual artists based in a Creative Europe country\nAw
 ard: Full financial support: travel\, shared accommodation in central Nico
 sia\, and daily allowance. Rehearsal space and full production support pro
 vided\; final live concert recorded (video and audio) for documentation an
 d international visibility.\nDuration: 31-day residency\, 23 October to 22
  November 2026\n\nMore: https://on-the-move.org/news/atheras-nicosia-ludic
 -lab-composers-new-works-toyful-music-festival-2026-cyprus?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://on-the-move.org/news/atheras-nicosia-ludic-lab-composers-new-wo
 rks-toyful-music-festival-2026-cyprus?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nicosia\, Cyprus\; open to individual artists based in a Creative 
 Europe country
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ditrapano-finch-manuscript-lab-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260710
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260711
SUMMARY:Deadline: Giancarlo DiTrapano Foundation: The Finch Manuscript Lab 
 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Finch Manuscript Lab is a 2.5-month residency supporting wr
 iters completing book-length manuscripts\, hosted at the Finch Country Hou
 se in Serramezzana\, Italy\, and designed as the final sprint in the marat
 hon of writing a book. It offers living and work space\, writing time in a
  tranquil setting\, creative community\, and professional development incl
 uding manuscript consultations\, craft discussions\, and publishing semina
 rs. Residency dates: 1 October to 15 December 2026\; residents will be sel
 ected by 30 July 2026. FUNDING: thanks to the support of the Goethe Instit
 ute and Culture Moves Europe\, all selected residents receive a stipend of
  EUR 2\,280 for the residency period (EUR 30 per day in residence\, paid w
 eekly)\, a travel allowance of EUR 400 for distances under 5\,000 km from 
 Serramezzana or EUR 800 for distances over 5\,000 km\, an additional EUR 4
 00 for green travel (e.g. taking trains instead of planes)\, and additiona
 l support of EUR 200 for parents of children under 18. ELIGIBILITY: applic
 ants must be over 18 and a legal resident of one of the 39 Culture Moves E
 urope eligible countries\, excluding Italy\; this includes all EU member s
 tates other than Italy and 13 participating non-EU countries (Albania\, An
 dorra\, Armenia\, Bosnia and Herzegovina\, Georgia\, Iceland\, Kosovo\, Mo
 ldova\, Montenegro\, North Macedonia\, Norway\, Serbia\, and Tunisia). APP
 LICATION (via Submittable\, in order of importance): a short sample of pas
 t work (any length\, though only the first 30 pages may be read)\; a brief
  note\, up to one page\, explaining the manuscript or book project to be w
 orked on in residency\, where you are in the creation process\, and why yo
 u are interested\; an excerpt of the book project not exceeding 30 pages (
 prose\, poetry\, mixed media\, photography\, or any other form of artist's
  book is acceptable)\; and a CV in English. NOTE ON DEADLINE: the foundati
 on's text gives the open call as 15 June to 10 July 2026\, while the Submi
 ttable page lists a close of Wednesday 15 July 2026 at 12:00 PM\; apply by
  10 July to be safe.\n\nOrganisation: The Giancarlo DiTrapano Foundation f
 or Literature and the Arts\nLocation: Finch Country House\, Serramezzana\,
  Italy\; open to legal residents of the 39 Culture Moves Europe eligible c
 ountries\, excluding Italy\nAward: EUR 2\,280 stipend for the residency pe
 riod (EUR 30 per day in residence\, paid weekly)\, plus travel allowance o
 f EUR 400 (under 5\,000 km) or EUR 800 (over 5\,000 km)\, an additional EU
 R 400 green-travel top-up (e.g. trains instead of planes)\, and EUR 200 ad
 ditional support for parents of children under 18. Supported by the Goethe
  Institute and Culture Moves Europe.\nDuration: 2.5 months\, 1 October to 
 15 December 2026\n\nMore: https://ditrapanofoundation.submittable.com/subm
 it/171cc54d-b582-47a3-93a4-47c46b65904b/the-finch-manuscript-lab?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ditrapanofoundation.submittable.com/submit/171cc54d-b582-47a3-9
 3a4-47c46b65904b/the-finch-manuscript-lab?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Finch Country House\, Serramezzana\, Italy\; open to legal residen
 ts of the 39 Culture Moves Europe eligible countries\, excluding Italy
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ramdam-extended-possibilities-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260714
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260715
SUMMARY:Deadline: RAMDAM\, un centre d'art: Extended Possibilities Residenc
 y 2027
DESCRIPTION:Extended Possibilities gives artists the opportunity to work on
  site at RAMDAM\, un centre d'art for 45 days\, a long period allowing the
 m to benefit from technical support and to present ongoing work to the pub
 lic. Artists receive on-site accommodation (a collective room for the whol
 e 45 days)\, access to a well-maintained\, up-to-date technical facility\,
  a grant to support their work\, and a lump-sum allowance for travel and v
 isas. RAMDAM is an activist space supporting artists in their artistic res
 earch\; residencies are open to artists or teams engaged in creation\, res
 earch\, or experimentation\, with no obligation to produce a finished work
 : dance\, theatre\, performance\, painting\, sculpture\, drawing\, film\, 
 video\, literary writing\, screenwriting\, digital art\, and hybrid forms 
 are all welcome. The call focuses on multidisciplinary projects and resear
 ch that break down barriers between disciplines and challenge their own fi
 eld of practice\, and considerable attention is given to how the work fits
  into a social and/or political context and resonates with our times. THE 
 CALL SUPPORTS: 1 or 2 artistic teams (RAMDAM can host at most 5 artists)\;
  performing artists of all disciplines\; projects at early stages of resea
 rch-creation and/or more advanced (residencies can be writing residencies 
 and/or stage residencies). All artists must be available for the full 45 d
 ays from 1 February to 15 March 2027 and must be from eligible countries (
 EU countries\, outermost regions\, overseas countries and territories\, an
 d some non-EU countries)\; artists from mainland (hexagonal) France cannot
  apply. The working and living spaces are wheelchair accessible\, though r
 eaching RAMDAM by public transport can be difficult for disabled people\; 
 accessibility support is available via Culture Moves Europe for residents 
 with disabilities. ALLOWANCES: EUR 1\,350 per resident for subsistence\; t
 ravel allowance EUR 400 under 5\,000 km or EUR 800 from 5\,000 km (travel 
 under 600 km must be by green means of transport unless disability or isla
 nd residence requires otherwise)\; green mobility top-up EUR 400 per resid
 ent for non-plane travel over 600 km\; visa top-up EUR 120\; outermost reg
 ions/OCT top-up EUR 175\; family top-up EUR 200 per child under 18 (housin
 g capacity is limited). TO APPLY: applications in English or French\; down
 load the residency project and administrative form documents and email the
  complete application to contact@ramdamcda.org with subject line 'extended
  possibilities - 2027' (no WeTransfer\, no important information in the em
 ail body\; reduce file sizes\; a third document may be added to help under
 stand the work). Confirmation within 7 working days\; shortlisted applican
 ts have video calls with the residency committee in mid-August. Deadline: 
 Tuesday 14 July 2026\, 11:59 p.m. NOTE: the call is arbitrarily limited to
  the first 40 applications received (still open as of 1 July 2026)\, so ap
 ply early. Made possible by the European programme Culture Moves Europe.\n
 \nOrganisation: RAMDAM\, un centre d'art\nLocation: Sainte-Foy-les-Lyon (n
 ear Lyon)\, France\; open to artists legally resident in Culture Moves Eur
 ope eligible countries (EU member states\, outermost regions\, overseas co
 untries and territories\, and some non-EU countries)\; artists from mainla
 nd (hexagonal) France cannot apply\nAward: EUR 1\,350 per resident allowan
 ce for subsistence and other costs\, plus travel allowance of EUR 400 (und
 er 5\,000 km) or EUR 800 (from 5\,000 km). Top-ups: green mobility EUR 400
  per resident (600 km or more by non-plane transport)\, visa EUR 120\, out
 ermost regions/OCT EUR 175\, family EUR 200 per child under 18. On-site ac
 commodation and technical facilities provided. Supported by Culture Moves 
 Europe.\nDuration: 45 days\, 1 February to 15 March 2027\n\nMore: https://
 ramdamcda.org/actualite-ramdam/extended-possibilities-residency-call?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ramdamcda.org/actualite-ramdam/extended-possibilities-residency
 -call?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Sainte-Foy-les-Lyon (near Lyon)\, France\; open to artists legally
  resident in Culture Moves Europe eligible countries (EU member states\, o
 utermost regions\, overseas countries and territories\, and some non-EU co
 untries)\; artists from mainland (hexagonal) France cannot apply
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:loghaven-artist-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260715
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260716
SUMMARY:Deadline: Loghaven Artist Residency
DESCRIPTION:Loghaven Artist Residency offers practicing artists time\, spac
 e\, and resources on ninety wooded acres in Knoxville\, Tennessee. Fellows
  stay in five rehabilitated historic log cabins with access to purpose-bui
 lt studio space. Each Fellow receives an USD 850 weekly living stipend\, a
  travel subsidy on a sliding scale from USD 400 to 800\, up to USD 200 in 
 materials shipping reimbursement\, and covered room and board. Residencies
  run from 2 to 6 weeks across sessions scheduled throughout 2027. The prog
 ram is open to artists at any career stage working in architecture\, dance
 \, interdisciplinary art\, music composition\, theater\, visual art\, and 
 writing\, including collaborative groups of up to nine people. Applicants 
 must be at least 21\, live more than 120 miles from Knoxville\, and be eli
 gible to work legally in the US\; international artists and degree-seeking
  students are not eligible.\n\nOrganisation: Loghaven Artist Residency\nLo
 cation: Knoxville\, Tennessee\, USA\nAward: USD 850 weekly living stipend\
 , travel subsidy USD 400 to 800\, up to USD 200 materials shipping reimbur
 sement\, plus room and board\, housing in historic log cabins\, and studio
  space USD 25 non-refundable application fee (fee waiver available on requ
 est)\nDuration: 2 to 6 weeks depending on session\n\nMore: https://loghave
 n.org/residencies/apply/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
URL:https://loghaven.org/residencies/apply/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Knoxville\, Tennessee\, USA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jentel-artist-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Jentel Artist Residency
DESCRIPTION:The Jentel Artist Residency offers approximately three-week res
 idencies in the foothills of the Bighorn Mountains near Banner\, Wyoming\,
  giving artists\, writers\, and composers dedicated time for creative work
 . Sessions run from mid-January through early December\, hosting six resid
 ents at a time. It is open to visual artists in any medium\, writers of fi
 ction\, creative nonfiction\, or poetry\, and composers across musical gen
 res. Residents receive a private bedroom\, a separate studio\, shared livi
 ng and kitchen space\, and a USD 100 weekly stipend to help cover food and
  personal expenses. Applicants must be at least 25 years old and be U.S. c
 itizens or foreign nationals whose primary residence is in the U.S. during
  the application year\, and may not be enrolled full-time in a degree prog
 ram. There is a USD 30 non-refundable application fee\, with deadlines of 
 September 15 for Winter and Spring sessions and January 15 for Summer and 
 Fall sessions.\n\nOrganisation: Jentel Foundation\nLocation: Banner\, Wyom
 ing\, USA\nAward: USD 100 weekly stipend (about USD 300 total over three w
 eeks)\, plus private bedroom\, separate studio space\, and shared living a
 nd kitchen facilities provided at no cost USD 30 application fee\nDuration
 : Approximately 3 weeks (arrive on the 15th\, depart the morning of the 7t
 h of the following month)\n\nMore: https://www.jentelarts.org/apply?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.jentelarts.org/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Banner\, Wyoming\, USA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hayama-artist-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Hayama Artist Residency
DESCRIPTION:The Hayama Artist Residency introduces visual artists from arou
 nd the world to Japanese culture and offers them their first gallery exhib
 ition in Japan. The four-week residency takes place in Hayama\, a coastal 
 town in Kanagawa Prefecture about 1.5 hours from Tokyo. Selected artists r
 eceive roundtrip airfare to Tokyo\, shared accommodation with one other re
 sident\, and USD 800 for meals and local transportation. A core element is
  a group exhibition during the stay\, hosted in partnership with KOKI ARTS
 \, a contemporary gallery in the Bakurocho art district of Tokyo. The prog
 ram is open to visual artists over 21 working in any medium\, based anywhe
 re in the world\, and applications are reviewed by the director and an int
 ernational selection committee. The June 2027 cycle has an application dea
 dline of September 30\, 2026\, with notification by December 15\, 2026.\n\
 nOrganisation: Hayama Artist Residency\nLocation: Hayama\, Kanagawa Prefec
 ture\, Japan\nAward: Fully funded: roundtrip airfare to Tokyo (Narita or H
 aneda)\, shared accommodation for 4 weeks\, and USD 800 for meals and loca
 l transportation. Group exhibition at KOKI ARTS gallery in Tokyo. USD 95 a
 pplication fee for first-time applicants\nDuration: 4 weeks\n\nMore: https
 ://www.hayamaresidency.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
URL:https://www.hayamaresidency.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hayama\, Kanagawa Prefecture\, Japan
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:simons-foundation-open-interval-turbulence-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Open Interval: An Artist-Scientist Exploration of Turbule
 nce
DESCRIPTION:Open Interval is a Simons Foundation program that supports trio
 s consisting of an artist\, a scientist\, and a representative from a 501(
 c)(3) arts organization to collaborate around a shared scientific theme. T
 he current cycle centers on the theme of turbulence\, a phenomenon at the 
 edge of chaos and beauty. Awarded trios receive USD 30\,000 to support a s
 ustained period of thought partnership and exploration rather than the pro
 duction of finished works or exhibitions. The program runs from April to D
 ecember 2027 with a touchstone meeting in May 2027 and possible cohort con
 venings. Trio members must be regionally co-located anywhere in the United
  States so they can collaborate in person. The scientist should hold a Ph.
 D. and be conducting basic research\, with priority given to fields such a
 s astrophysics\, neuroscience\, quantum physics\, biology\, or mathematics
 . The application portal opens September 9\, 2026\, and all three trio mem
 bers must submit for the application to be complete.\n\nOrganisation: Simo
 ns Foundation\nLocation: United States (trio must be regionally co-located
 )\nAward: USD 30\,000 per awarded trio\nDuration: April to December 2027 (
 several months of collaboration)\n\nMore: https://www.simonsfoundation.org
 /2026/06/01/coming-soon-open-interval-an-artist-scientist-exploration-of-t
 urbulence/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.simonsfoundation.org/2026/06/01/coming-soon-open-interval-a
 n-artist-scientist-exploration-of-turbulence/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:United States (trio must be regionally co-located)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:studios-at-mass-moca-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Studios at MASS MoCA Residencies
DESCRIPTION:The Studios at MASS MoCA is a year-round residency program on t
 he museum's campus in North Adams\, Massachusetts\, hosting up to 10 artis
 ts at a time for stays of two or four weeks. It primarily welcomes visual 
 artists across all media and writers in all literary disciplines\, and app
 licants from around the world are encouraged to apply. Residents receive 2
 4-hour access to a private furnished studio\, lodging in nearby apartments
 \, and several communal meals each week\, plus museum membership benefits 
 and access to The Clark Art Institute. The program offers need-based finan
 cial aid (artists typically pay between USD 0 and USD 450 per week) and fu
 lly funded fellowships that cover all residency fees for up to four weeks.
  General application deadlines fall on May 1 and November 1 each year\, an
 d the application is free to submit.\n\nOrganisation: MASS MoCA (Massachus
 etts Museum of Contemporary Art)\nLocation: North Adams\, Massachusetts\, 
 USA\nAward: Provides private 24/7 studio space\, furnished housing\, and s
 even communal meals per week. Financial aid is available so artists reques
 ting it typically pay between USD 0 and USD 450 per week\, and fully funde
 d fellowships cover all residency fees for up to four weeks. Artists who f
 ully self-fund pay a subsidized rate of USD 650 per week.\nDuration: 2 or 
 4 weeks\n\nMore: https://massmoca.org/studios/?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://massmoca.org/studios/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
LOCATION:North Adams\, Massachusetts\, USA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a-wrinkle-in-thyme-farm-fiber-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: Farm\, Flock and Fiber Artist in Residence
DESCRIPTION:A Wrinkle in Thyme Farm is a small\, women-owned diversified fa
 rm in Sumner\, Maine that offers a six-month live-in fiber arts residency 
 starting in May. The resident exchanges an average of 15 to 20 hours per w
 eek of farm work for a modest monthly stipend\, free private rustic housin
 g\, community meals\, farm-grown food\, and access to the fiber studio. Re
 sidents receive solo studio time plus one day a week of learning and colla
 boration with fiber artist Marty Elkin\, working with home-grown Maine woo
 l through felting\, dyeing\, knitting and spinning. The program also inclu
 des training in flock management\, animal husbandry and lamb care\, with t
 he option to add two months for lambing season. It is designed for emergin
 g fiber artists who are single females able to lift 50 pounds and work aro
 und a farm. Applications open in November with a December 31 deadline and 
 a non-refundable USD 25 application fee.\n\nOrganisation: A Wrinkle in Thy
 me Farm\nLocation: Sumner\, Maine\, USA\nAward: Modest monthly stipend (ar
 ound USD 400/month) in exchange for roughly 15 to 20 hours/week of farm wo
 rk\, plus free rustic private housing (solar power\, wood stove)\, shared 
 kitchen\, bath and WiFi\, community meals and farm-grown food\, dedicated 
 solo studio time\, and weekly collaboration with resident fiber artist Mar
 ty Elkin. USD 25 non-refundable application fee\nDuration: Six months begi
 nning in May\, with an optional two additional months for lambing and earl
 y lamb care\n\nMore: https://www.awrinkleinthymefarm.com/?page_id=1294&utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.awrinkleinthymefarm.com/?page_id=1294&utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Sumner\, Maine\, USA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:helene-wurlitzer-foundation-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270119
SUMMARY:Deadline: Helene Wurlitzer Foundation Residency
DESCRIPTION:The Helene Wurlitzer Foundation of New Mexico runs one of the o
 ldest artist residency programs in the United States\, established in 1954
 \, on a 15-acre campus in Taos\, New Mexico. The residency is open to visu
 al artists\, literary artists\, and music composers\, including painters\,
  sculptors\, photographers\, filmmakers\, writers\, poets\, playwrights\, 
 screenwriters\, and songwriters. Selected grantees receive rent-free and u
 tility-paid housing in a furnished casita for a session of 10 to 12 weeks\
 , with access to a Commons House offering WiFi\, a library\, and bicycles.
  No stipend is provided in most cases\, and residents cover their own food
  and transportation. Applications are open to creative artists worldwide r
 egardless of age\, experience\, or nationality\, and the annual deadline i
 s January 18 for residencies the following calendar year. There is a non-w
 aivable USD 30 application fee.\n\nOrganisation: The Helene Wurlitzer Foun
 dation of New Mexico\nLocation: Taos\, New Mexico\, USA\nAward: Rent-free\
 , utility-paid furnished housing (casita)\; no stipend (rare stipend suppo
 rt via the Rhonda Artist Stipend Fund)\; artists cover food and travel USD
  30 application fee\nDuration: 10 to 12 weeks (Sessions 1 and 3 are 12 wee
 ks\, Session 2 is 10 weeks)\n\nMore: https://wurlitzerfoundation.org/apply
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://wurlitzerfoundation.org/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Taos\, New Mexico\, USA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kala-fellowship-program-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270301
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270302
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kala Fellowship Program
DESCRIPTION:The Kala Fellowship Program supports international\, national\,
  and local artists producing innovative work in and across multiple media\
 , with an emphasis on Kala's specialized printmaking\, photography\, and d
 igital media equipment. The institute supports up to 6 artists per cycle w
 ith a USD 3\,000 stipend\, 24/7 access to its Berkeley facilities for 1 to
  9 months\, one month of housing for artists based outside the 9 Bay Area 
 counties\, a Kala class or workshop\, and a culminating group show in the 
 Kala Gallery. Applications are submitted through kala.slideroom.com and re
 quire a statement of interest\, an artist CV\, documentation of 5 to 10 re
 cent works\, and two references. Artists enrolled in a degree-granting pro
 gram during the fellowship period are not eligible. The application opens 
 in December with no fee through January 15\, after which a USD 25 applicat
 ion fee applies through the March 1 deadline.\n\nOrganisation: Kala Art In
 stitute\nLocation: Berkeley\, California\, USA\nAward: USD 3\,000 stipend\
 , 24/7 facility access for 1 to 9 months\, 1 month of housing for artists 
 outside the 9 Bay Area counties\, a Kala class or workshop\, and a group e
 xhibition USD 25 application fee (free if applying December through Januar
 y 15)\nDuration: 1 to 9 months within the July 2026 to June 2027 fellowshi
 p period\n\nMore: https://www.kala.org/residencies/fellowship-program/?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.kala.org/residencies/fellowship-program/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berkeley\, California\, USA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:roswell-artist-in-residence-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270315
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270316
SUMMARY:Deadline: Roswell Artist-in-Residence Program
DESCRIPTION:The Roswell Artist-in-Residence Program\, established in 1967 a
 nd run by The RAiR Foundation\, offers visual artists a year-long studio-b
 ased residency known as the Gift of Time. Each resident receives a private
  house and a studio on a fifty-acre complex\, with rent\, utilities\, repa
 irs\, and maintenance covered by the program. Artists also receive a month
 ly stipend of USD 1\,100 plus a USD 250 monthly materials stipend. The pro
 gram is open to professional visual artists aged 21 and older working in p
 ainting\, drawing\, sculpture\, printmaking\, photography\, video\, digita
 l media\, and installation. It does not support performance art\, writing\
 , music\, or production crafts. The application period for the next cycle 
 runs from January 1 to March 15\, 2027\, and international applicants are 
 accepted with visa support available.\n\nOrganisation: The RAiR Foundation
 \nLocation: Roswell\, New Mexico\, USA\nAward: USD 1\,100 per month stipen
 d\, plus USD 250 per month materials stipend from the Frederick Hammersley
  Foundation. Includes a private house and a studio with rent\, utilities\,
  repairs\, and maintenance covered. USD 26.32 application fee\nDuration: 1
 2 months (one year)\n\nMore: https://www.rair.org/application-info?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.rair.org/application-info?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Roswell\, New Mexico\, USA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cmrfe-multispecies-residency-autumn-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260705
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260706
SUMMARY:Deadline: Artist Residency Autumn 2026 (Centre for Multispecies Rel
 ations and Future Ecologies\, Palermo)
DESCRIPTION:The Centre for Multispecies Relations and Future Ecologies invi
 tes applications from two artists for a 62-day residency (12 October - 12 
 December 2026) at its site in the Altarello di Baida district of Palermo\,
  Sicily. The residency is structured around a 1\,500 sqm garden at the thr
 eshold between the city's urban expansion and the historic rural landscape
  of the surrounding hills\; the site\, degraded through previous use (soil
  compaction and significant biodiversity loss)\, functions as both studio 
 and subject\, and artists participate in an ongoing process of ecological 
 transformation\, producing interventions that emerge from extended observa
 tion and fieldwork. Applications are welcome across all mediums and discip
 lines (installation\, sound\, performance\, video\, food art\, participato
 ry practice\, and beyond)\; research-based and interdisciplinary practices
  are especially encouraged. The Centre works at the intersection of art\, 
 science\, and (agro)ecological practices\, with a focus on multispecies co
 existence and climate change in the Mediterranean\, and has been based in 
 Palermo since 2021. PROGRAMME: five phases (orientation with small trips a
 nd gatherings\; observation with independent fieldwork and consultations w
 ith artists\, curators\, scientists\, and anthropologists\; proposal and e
 cological feasibility developed with mentors\; creation\; and public resti
 tution with an open event\, a workshop\, and a public discussion). Each ar
 tist develops an independent site-specific intervention\; the two resident
 s share the site\, living space\, and process\, with exchange encouraged b
 ut not prescribed. Artist duos and artists who want to collaborate are enc
 ouraged to apply (you can apply as an individual for one position\, as a d
 uo for both\, or as two artists collaborating for two positions). Mentorsh
 ip by co-founders/artistic directors Fabio Aranzulla and Luca Cinquemani (
 weekly site visits\, studio discussions\, work-in-progress presentations)\
 ; logistics managed by Francesca Farris. WHO: artists whose work engages w
 ith ecology\, multispecies relations\, or the more-than-human\, who can mo
 ve between observation and making and are interested in dialogue with scie
 ntists\, land workers\, and local communities. Priority is given to artist
 s from working-class and less-privileged backgrounds\, those who self-iden
 tify as part of marginalised communities\, and candidates reflecting diver
 sity in gender\, age\, geographical background\, and ability\; green trave
 l is prioritised as a condition of participation where feasible. Applicant
 s should be open to living and working in a neighbourhood on the margins o
 f Palermo's periphery. Funded by Culture Moves Europe (Creative Europe pro
 gramme of the European Union). APPLICATION: first phase via the online for
 m (opened 10 June)\; shortlisted artists contacted before the end of July\
 ; second phase is video calls with shortlisted candidates\; applications a
 ccepted in English and Italian. Contact: contact.cmrfe@gmail.com. Deadline
  5 July 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Centre for Multispecies Relations and Futur
 e Ecologies\nLocation: Altarello di Baida district\, Palermo\, Sicily\, It
 aly. On-site 62-day residency\, 12 October - 12 December 2026. Open to all
  nationalities\, but applicants must be officially residing in a Creative 
 Europe country (excluding Italy).\nAward: Total allowance of EUR 1\,860 (b
 efore tax) per artist\, plus a travel budget of EUR 400 per artist (for di
 stances under 4\,000 km) with a EUR 400 green-mobility top-up\, plus a pro
 duction budget. Also provided: on-site accommodation in a fully furnished 
 independent house (private bedroom\; shared kitchen\, living room\, two ba
 throoms\; outdoor studio space 100m from the working site)\, access to rec
 ycled/salvaged materials through the Centre's partnerships\, a bicycle per
  resident\, and a final public event.\nDuration: 62-day residency\, 12 Oct
 ober - 12 December 2026\, structured in five phases (orientation\, observa
 tion/fieldwork\, proposal and ecological feasibility\, creation\, and publ
 ic restitution).\n\nMore: https://tally.so/r/81r5Mz?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://tally.so/r/81r5Mz?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Altarello di Baida district\, Palermo\, Sicily\, Italy. On-site 62
 -day residency\, 12 October - 12 December 2026. Open to all nationalities\
 , but applicants must be officially residing in a Creative Europe country 
 (excluding Italy).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ted-posca-global-artist-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: TED & POSCA Global Artist Residency 2026: Visible Mending
DESCRIPTION:TED (the global platform for ideas and storytelling) and POSCA 
 (a creative brand by uni Brands Corporation) are launching a new kind of a
 rtist residency: a globally distributed cohort of artists working across d
 ifferent geographies\, cultures\, and communities\, united by a shared dri
 ve to shape public life through art. Fine Acts\, the external curatorial p
 artner selected by TED & POSCA\, leads the curation\, creative direction\,
  and coordination. There is no single location and no central studio: sele
 cted artists work within their own communities\, following a shared creati
 ve constraint (a unifying conceptual framework around repair\, hope\, and 
 beauty)\, with projects unfolding in public space\, community participatio
 n as a key part of the work\, and process mattering as much as outcome. 20
 26 THEME\, VISIBLE MENDING: inspired in part by Kintsugi (the Japanese pra
 ctice of repairing broken ceramics with gold)\, the theme explores repair 
 as a creative and civic act\, inviting artists to consider how wounds\, ru
 ptures\, and imperfections can become sites of transformation\, and to mak
 e processes of repair visible through public interventions that spark refl
 ection\, dialogue\, and collective imagination. In 2026\, four artists wil
 l be selected to develop community-rooted public interventions to be imple
 mented in 2027. AWARD: each selected artist receives a total of USD 15\,00
 0 to cover artist fees\, production costs/community activation\, and docum
 entation\, plus a production budget and tools from POSCA\, creative direct
 ion and storytelling support\, and visibility through TED and Fine Acts' g
 lobal platforms. While the residency term is one year\, the initiative wil
 l run for multiple years (2027\, 2028\, 2029)\, expanding the cohort year 
 by year and building an evolving global archive of civic artistic interven
 tions. Apply by 31 July 2026.\n\nOrganisation: TED & POSCA (curated by Fin
 e Acts)\nLocation: Globally distributed\; no single location or central st
 udio. Selected artists work within their own communities\, with projects u
 nfolding in public space.\nAward: Each selected artist receives a total of
  USD 15\,000 (covering artist fees\, production costs/community activation
 \, and documentation)\, plus a production budget and tools from POSCA\, cr
 eative direction and storytelling support\, and visibility through TED and
  Fine Acts' global platforms.\nDuration: One-year residency term\; communi
 ty-rooted public interventions developed in 2026 for implementation in 202
 7. The initiative runs for multiple years (2027\, 2028\, 2029)\, expanding
  the cohort year by year.\n\nMore: https://fineacts.co/ted-posca-residency
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fineacts.co/ted-posca-residency?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Globally distributed\; no single location or central studio. Selec
 ted artists work within their own communities\, with projects unfolding in
  public space.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wassaic-project-2027-summer-exhibition-open-call@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260810
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260811
SUMMARY:Deadline: Wassaic Project 2027 Summer Exhibition Open Call
DESCRIPTION:The Wassaic Project is holding its annual Open Call for the 202
 7 Summer Exhibition\, for artists of all mediums\, including 2D work\, scu
 lpture\, video\, new media\, site-specific installation\, performance\, te
 xt\, poems\, essays\, and publication-specific work. Selected work is show
 cased alongside a diverse range of pieces and performances in and around h
 istoric Wassaic and Maxon Mills\; the 2027 Summer Exhibition will be free 
 and open to the public every weekend from 1 May to 12 September 2027. In a
 n effort toward W.A.G.E. certification\, all accepted artists receive a mo
 dest honorarium to participate. Artists interested in creating a site-spec
 ific installation are also eligible for an Exhibitions Fellowship to help 
 realize their work\; Fellows are offered a no-fee residency for 1-4 weeks 
 in April or May 2027 (artists interested in making site-specific work shou
 ld still apply regardless of whether they are interested in or able to be 
 in residence). The Wassaic Project cultivates and supports community for e
 merging and professional contemporary artists\, writers\, and other creati
 ves\, with a residency program housed in historic landmark buildings that 
 hosts 10 artists each month in the heart of a rural community. APPLICATION
 : requires application forms\, a CV\, and an artwork/portfolio\; submitted
  via SlideRoom. Application fee: USD 25 (no participation fee or additiona
 l fees). Deadline 10 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: The Wassaic Project\nLo
 cation: Wassaic\, New York\, United States (in and around historic Wassaic
  and Maxon Mills).\nAward: A modest honorarium for all accepted artists (p
 art of the organization's effort toward W.A.G.E. certification). Artists c
 reating site-specific installations are also eligible for an Exhibitions F
 ellowship and a no-fee residency of 1-4 weeks in April or May 2027.\nDurat
 ion: The 2027 Summer Exhibition runs free and open to the public every wee
 kend\, 1 May to 12 September 2027. Optional fellowship residency of 1-4 we
 eks in April or May 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.wassaicproject.org/apply/su
 mmer-exhibition-faq?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
URL:https://www.wassaicproject.org/apply/summer-exhibition-faq?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Wassaic\, New York\, United States (in and around historic Wassaic
  and Maxon Mills).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:atu-windgate-artist-in-residence-fall-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260703
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260704
SUMMARY:Deadline: Windgate Artist-in-Residence Fall 2026 (Arkansas Tech Uni
 versity)
DESCRIPTION:The Artist-in-Residence (AIR) program at Arkansas Tech Universi
 ty is an immersive experience within an art and educational community\, in
 tended to advance the careers of practicing artists\, present residents as
  role models for the ATU community\, and strengthen public awareness of th
 e significance of making art and its effect on the surrounding community. 
 The residency takes place over a five-month period\, giving the artist tim
 e and space to focus on the creative process. For Fall 2026\, the program 
 will select an artist to create a public artwork that enhances the ATU cam
 pus\; both two-dimensional and three-dimensional proposals will be conside
 red. The program is supported by a generous grant from the Windgate Charit
 able Foundation. The Department of Art at ATU offers programs in Fine Art\
 , Graphic Design\, Game and Interactive Media Design\, and Art Education\,
  with a facility in Norman Hall featuring a professional gallery\, compute
 r lab\, lecture hall\, and studios for painting\, drawing\, printmaking\, 
 sculpture\, ceramics\, and graphic design. RESIDENCY DETAILS & EXPECTATION
 S: residents must be artists with significant exhibition records\, strong 
 communication skills\, sustained studio practice\, and a desire to engage 
 with the larger campus community\; involvement may include guest lecturing
 \, public talks\, mentoring students\, open studios\, and/or collaborating
  with faculty and students. The resident sometimes teaches one course in 2
 D Design\, 3D Design\, or Introduction to Drawing during their stay when e
 nrollment allows. Artists are expected to commit as a full-time resident f
 or the Fall academic term 2026. BENEFITS: USD 30\,000 stipend (minus fring
 es)\, USD 18\,000 for supplies\, a 2-bed/2-bath campus apartment\, and a l
 arge climate-controlled off-campus studio. Deadline 3 July 2026.\n\nOrgani
 sation: Arkansas Tech University (supported by the Windgate Charitable Fou
 ndation)\nLocation: Russellville\, Arkansas\, United States (Russellville 
 campus\, in the Arkansas River Valley\, about one hour from Little Rock). 
 In-person\, full-time residency.\nAward: USD 30\,000 stipend (minus fringe
 s) plus USD 18\,000 for supplies. Housing provided (a 2-bed\, 2-bath campu
 s apartment) and a large\, climate-controlled\, dedicated off-campus studi
 o space.\nDuration: Five-month residency over the Fall academic term 2026.
 \n\nMore: https://www.atu.edu/academicaffairs/faculty/adjunct/docs/AIR%20A
 D%20FALL%202026.pdf?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
URL:https://www.atu.edu/academicaffairs/faculty/adjunct/docs/AIR%20AD%20FAL
 L%202026.pdf?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Russellville\, Arkansas\, United States (Russellville campus\, in 
 the Arkansas River Valley\, about one hour from Little Rock). In-person\, 
 full-time residency.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:neiu-art-design-studio-art-residency-2026-2027@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260809
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260810
SUMMARY:Deadline: NEIU Art + Design Studio Art Residency 2026-2027
DESCRIPTION:The NEIU Art + Design Studio Art Residency strives to create vi
 sible connections between Northeastern Illinois University's diverse popul
 ation of art and design students and working artists who embody these iden
 tities\, providing insights and inspiration through a dynamic exchange of 
 ideas and techniques. Visiting Artists should demonstrate a commitment to 
 their artistic practice and an interest in engaging with NEIU's students a
 nd creative community. Each Visiting Artist is awarded an honorarium and h
 as full access for a semester to the NEIU Art + Design facilities specific
  to their project\; over the residency they showcase their work in a publi
 c academic forum\, lead a hands-on workshop\, and participate in a Portfol
 io Review Day for NEIU's Art + Design students. FACILITIES (in the Salme H
 arju Steinberg Fine Arts Center) include a Design Studio with the largest 
 collection of Riso drums at any Chicago university\, a Fab Lab (FDM and re
 sin 3D printers\, large-format CNC router\, vinyl cutters\, laser cutters)
 \, a Ceramic Studio (throwing wheels\, glaze room\, electric and gas kilns
 \, raku area)\, a Letterpress Studio (two Vandercook presses\, metal and w
 ood type)\, a Sculpture Studio (wood shop\, clay modeling and spray painti
 ng areas)\, a Photography Studio (analog and digital\, plus a lighting stu
 dio)\, and fully equipped Painting\, Drawing\, and Printmaking studios. BE
 NEFITS: USD 800 honorarium\; facility access based on project focus (Art +
  Tech\, Ceramics\, Drawing\, Painting\, Photography\, Printmaking\, Sculpt
 ure)\, with supplies requestable subject to approval\; and the opportunity
  to exhibit in a group exhibition in the NEIU Fine Arts Center Gallery. PA
 RTICIPATION: lead a 2-hour hands-on workshop for 15-20 students on a topic
  relevant to the project\; give an hour-long artist talk with Q&A\; and se
 rve as a guest panelist for a day-long portfolio review. KEY DATES: open c
 all 2 June - 9 August\; emailed acceptances in October\; Residency Session
  1 runs 25 January - 14 May and Session 2 runs 30 August - 11 December. Ap
 ply via the JotForm application. Deadline 9 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: 
 Northeastern Illinois University (NEIU)\, Art + Design Department\nLocatio
 n: Salme Harju Steinberg Fine Arts Center\, Northeastern Illinois Universi
 ty\, Chicago\, Illinois\, United States. In-person\; semester-long access 
 to NEIU facilities.\nAward: USD 800 honorarium\, plus a semester of full a
 ccess to NEIU Art + Design facilities specific to the project (Art + Tech\
 , Ceramics\, Drawing\, Painting\, Photography\, Printmaking\, Sculpture)\;
  supplies can be requested with guidance and approval from Studio Area per
 sonnel. Visiting Artists may also exhibit in a group exhibition in the NEI
 U Fine Arts Center Gallery.\nDuration: One semester. Residency Session 1: 
 25 January - 14 May\; Session 2: 30 August - 11 December.\n\nMore: https:/
 /form.jotform.com/261044627286156?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
