BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wsw-artists-book-residency-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Deadline: WSW Artist's Book Residency Grant
DESCRIPTION:Women's Studio Workshop (WSW) offers an eight- to ten-week resi
 dency for artists to produce a limited-edition artist's book. Working inte
 nsively in WSW's studios in Rosendale\, NY\, selected artists print and bi
 nd their own books\; edition size must be between 50 and 100 copies. AMOUN
 T: $350/week stipend\; up to $1\,000 for materials\; up to $250 for travel
  within the Continental US\; free onsite housing\; 24/7 studio access. WSW
  provides technical advice\, training on new equipment\, techniques\, and 
 materials\, and production assistance. SALES CONTRACT: 20% of the edition 
 goes to the artist\; 20% (at least nine copies) stays with WSW for archiva
 l and institutional sales\; 60% goes to general distribution and sale. If 
 the artist sells through WSW\, WSW takes a 30% commission plus 20% for mar
 keting\; the artist receives a 50% commission\, paid annually around 30 Ju
 ne. WSW holds the right to sell distribution copies at a 20% discount to s
 tanding-order and repository institutions. WSW's books are held in over 45
 0 collections worldwide\, including the Library of Congress\, Yale Univers
 ity\, and Vassar College. An outside jury of artists and curators selects 
 recipients. INDIGENOUS ARTISTS: applicants may check the appropriate box o
 n the Submittable form to be considered for the BIMA Artist's Book Residen
 cy Grant for Indigenous Artists. APPLICATION MATERIALS (upload via Submitt
 able): current resume\; brief project description including media required
  (200-word maximum)\; materials budget form (Google Sheets\, Excel\, or PD
 F)\; up to ten images of recent work\; image script (title\, medium\, dime
 nsions\, date). MAILED MATERIALS (to WSW at the address below): a physical
  book mock-up demonstrating how the book will be bound or function\, actua
 l size\, with at least 1-2 fully realised spreads\; and the shipping form 
 (download and open the PDF locally). Mail to: Artist's Book Application\, 
 Women's Studio Workshop\, PO Box 489\, Rosendale\, NY 12472. Applications 
 open 1 August 2026\; deadline 15 November 2026\, 11:59pm EST\; notificatio
 n March 2027\; residency runs September through June\, one year after appl
 ication. Apply via Submittable at https://wsworkshop.org/residencies/artis
 ts-book-residency-grant/.\n\nOrganisation: Women's Studio Workshop (WSW)\n
 Location: Rosendale\, NY\, USA\; in-person residency.\nAward: $350/week st
 ipend\; up to $1\,000 for materials\; up to $250 for travel within the Con
 tinental US\; free onsite housing\; 24/7 studio access. No application fee
 .\nDuration: 8-10 weeks\; residency runs September through June\, one year
  after application.\n\nMore: https://wsworkshop.org/residencies/artists-bo
 ok-residency-grant/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
URL:https://wsworkshop.org/residencies/artists-book-residency-grant/?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Rosendale\, NY\, USA\; in-person residency.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:revitalizing-rituals-2026-open-call@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260719
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260720
SUMMARY:Deadline: Revitalizing Rituals 2026 Open Call
DESCRIPTION:Revitalizing Rituals invites artists from all disciplines -- so
 und\, movement\, visual arts\, installation\, performance\, and transdisci
 plinary practices -- to join a research-creation journey across two landsc
 apes: Bhar Lazreg in Tunisia and the wetlands of Somogy County in Hungary.
  The project explores rituals as living forms of belonging: reconnecting c
 ommunities\, land\, memory\, food\, ecological reciprocity\, and the more-
 than-human world. Selected artists work with local communities as co-parti
 cipants in a shared inquiry into moving from extraction toward reciprocity
 . Organised by Homo Faber Alapítvány (Hungary). AMOUNT: EUR 6\,000 gross
  artist fee and production budget\; international travel and per diems cov
 ered\; on-site accommodation provided. ELIGIBILITY: minimum 5 years of act
 ive artistic practice\; portfolio reflecting interest in situated or relat
 ional work\; no formal degree required\; working language is English (loca
 l language navigation valued)\; must be available for the full residency c
 ycle including all international travel\; must be able to legally receive 
 the fee and invoice the organising partners from country of residence. Str
 ongly encourages applications from historically marginalised or underrepre
 sented voices. KEY DATES: Application Deadline 19 July 2026 (midnight) -- 
 note the open call PDF also references a 5 July date\; the officially prom
 oted deadline is 19 July\; Online Q&A 29 June 2026\, 14:00 Tunisia / 15:00
  CET (register at https://forms.gle/brnZvXvFe4JB8zL26)\; Online Conversati
 ons with shortlisted artists: mid July to mid August 2026\; Selection Resu
 lts: 31 August 2026\; Placemaking Camp: 1 week\, end of November 2026\, Hu
 ngary\; Storytellers Camp: 1 week\, March 2027\, Tunisia\; Residency Perio
 d: minimum 1 month (splittable)\, April to July 2027\; Final Presentation:
  August 2027\; Closing Event: 3 days\, winter/early spring 2028\, Hungary.
  Apply via the open call form linked at https://homofaber.hu/wp-content/up
 loads/2026/06/Artist-Open-Call-FINAL-in-the-RR-form.pdf.\n\nOrganisation: 
 Homo Faber Alapítvány (Homo Faber Foundation)\nLocation: Bhar Lazreg\, T
 unisia and Somogy County\, Hungary\; multi-stage in-person residency acros
 s both sites.\nAward: EUR 6\,000 gross artist fee and production budget\; 
 international travel and per diems covered\; on-site accommodation provide
 d. No application fee.\nDuration: Multi-stage residency: Placemaking Camp 
 (1 week\, November 2026\, Hungary)\; Storytellers Camp (1 week\, March 202
 7\, Tunisia)\; Residency Period (minimum 1 month\, April-July 2027)\; publ
 ic presentation (August 2027)\; Closing Event (3 days\, winter/early sprin
 g 2028\, Hungary).\n\nMore: https://homofaber.hu/wp-content/uploads/2026/0
 6/Artist-Open-Call-FINAL-in-the-RR-form.pdf?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://homofaber.hu/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Artist-Open-Call-FINAL-
 in-the-RR-form.pdf?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
LOCATION:Bhar Lazreg\, Tunisia and Somogy County\, Hungary\; multi-stage in
 -person residency across both sites.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:she-got-game-emerging-talents-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Game Design Emerging Talents: She Got Game
DESCRIPTION:She Got Game is a Pro Helvetia mentoring programme promoting eq
 ual opportunities in the Swiss and international game industry\, supportin
 g the representation of women in management positions through dialogue wit
 h experienced international experts from the game industry. The call is ai
 med at professional game designers who identify as women from the regions 
 of Pro Helvetia's liaison offices: the Arab region\, East Asia\, South Ame
 rica\, South Asia and Vietnam\, and West\, Central\, East and Southern Afr
 ica. ELIGIBILITY: Emerging Talents are game developers or game studios who
 se relevant training or registration (self-employed\, sole proprietorship\
 , or company) dates back less than seven years. Selection criteria include
  digital content for devices such as computers\, consoles\, mobile devices
 \, or mixed-reality devices requiring a high level of interaction\; clearl
 y defined objectives in terms of participation and career\; originality\, 
 feasibility\, degree of innovation\, and marketability of the project\; an
 d project leaders holding the copyright and rights of use. Excluded: commi
 ssioned work and projects that are part of an advertising or promotional c
 ampaign\, and purely technological projects without obvious narrative and/
 or aesthetic content. WHAT IS OFFERED: individual coaching and input talks
  on project development\, business strategy and finances\, marketing\, PR\
 , and pitch training\; involvement in a growing community of female game d
 evelopers\; potential access to international trade fairs\; CHF 3\,000 tow
 ard the production of a prototype or demo version\; and up to CHF 250 per 
 week toward childcare or children's travel expenses when attending interna
 tional trade fairs (a budget must be presented in advance). All modules ar
 e conducted in English\; the programme is a time-consuming commitment of r
 oughly 30 hours over six months\, plus potential additional time attending
  events or trade fairs. APPLICATION: submit a short CV (including educatio
 n/training\, nationality\, and residency status in Switzerland)\, a short 
 description of the current project (type and genre\, gameplay\, platform\,
  development status\, target audience\, with relevant visual material\, ma
 x. 10 A4 pages)\, a project portfolio\, and expectations regarding the pro
 gramme's objectives. All documents should be submitted in English\; if not
  possible\, applications may be submitted in German\, French\, or Italian.
  KEY DATES: applications open 1 July 2026\; submission deadline 1 Septembe
 r 2026\, 23:59 CEST\; notification of decision in November 2026\; earliest
  project start 1 January 2027. Apply via the Pro Helvetia application port
 al.\n\nOrganisation: Pro Helvetia (Swiss Arts Council)\nLocation: Remote/i
 nternational mentoring programme\; applicants must be based in one of Pro 
 Helvetia's liaison-office regions (Arab region\, East Asia\, South America
 \, South Asia and Vietnam\, and West\, Central\, East and Southern Africa)
 .\nAward: CHF 3\,000 toward the production of a prototype or demo version\
 , plus individual coaching and community access\; potential access to inte
 rnational trade fairs. When attending trade fairs\, applicants with childc
 are responsibilities can request up to CHF 250 per week for childcare or c
 hildren's travel expenses. No application fee.\nDuration: Six-month mentor
 ing programme\, approximately 30 hours total commitment\; notification in 
 November 2026\; earliest project start 1 January 2027.\n\nMore: https://pr
 ohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/game-design-emerging-talents-she-got-game-3/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/game-design-emerging-talents-she
 -got-game-3/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote/international mentoring programme\; applicants must be base
 d in one of Pro Helvetia's liaison-office regions (Arab region\, East Asia
 \, South America\, South Asia and Vietnam\, and West\, Central\, East and 
 Southern Africa).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohelvetia-writing-in-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Writing in Residency
DESCRIPTION:Pro Helvetia's Writing in Residency programme provides residenc
 y opportunities (for example Traduki in Southeast Europe or Art Omi) for a
 uthors and translators to develop or research projects. Applicants must ha
 ve prior professionally published work. ELIGIBILITY: requires a connection
  to Switzerland (Swiss citizenship\, or permanent residency with regular a
 rtistic activity in Switzerland)\; not open to practitioners without a Swi
 ss connection. WHAT IS OFFERED: travel and accommodation costs (varying by
  destination)\, plus childcare support of up to CHF 1\,000 per month for a
 pplicants with caregiving responsibilities. Submission deadline 1 Septembe
 r (23:59 CEST). Apply via the Pro Helvetia portal.\n\nOrganisation: Pro He
 lvetia (Swiss Arts Council)\nLocation: Switzerland-based authors and trans
 lators\; residencies at partner locations abroad (e.g. Traduki in Southeas
 t Europe\, Art Omi).\nAward: Travel and accommodation costs (vary by desti
 nation)\; childcare support up to CHF 1\,000 per month for applicants with
  caregiving responsibilities. No application fee.\nDuration: Residency to 
 develop or research a project\; deadline 1 September.\n\nMore: https://pro
 helvetia.ch/en/find-support/writing-in-residency?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/writing-in-residency?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Switzerland-based authors and translators\; residencies at partner
  locations abroad (e.g. Traduki in Southeast Europe\, Art Omi).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wheeler-centre-next-chapter-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Wheeler Centre: The Next Chapter 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Next Chapter is The Wheeler Centre's flagship writing progr
 am\, designed to elevate Australian stories that are underrepresented and 
 to nurture a new wave of writers to tell them. Each fellow receives a AUD 
 $15\,000 stipend and is paired with a handpicked mentor for a twelve-month
  period to progress a major writing project. Fellows also receive a reside
 ncy at Varuna\, The National Writers' House\; an end-of-year publishing in
 tensive at The Wheeler Centre\; and meaningful opportunities to connect wi
 th peers\, agents\, publishers\, and readers. One fellowship place is dedi
 cated specifically to a poet: The Malcolm Robertson Fellowship. 2027 judge
 s: Melissa Lucashenko\, Micaela Sahhar\, Cher Tan\, and Melanie Saward. EL
 IGIBILITY: Australian writers. No specific genre restrictions stated\; the
  program focuses on stories that are not currently being told and voices t
 hat are underrepresented. TIMELINE: submissions open 2 June 2026\; submiss
 ions close 31 July 2026 (5pm)\; 2027 Next Chapter Fellows announced 10 Nov
 ember 2026. Questions: thenextchapter@wheelercentre.com. Apply at https://
 www.wheelercentre.com/the-next-chapter.\n\nOrganisation: The Wheeler Centr
 e\nLocation: Melbourne\, Australia\; includes residency at Varuna\, The Na
 tional Writers' House\, and an end-of-year publishing intensive at The Whe
 eler Centre.\nAward: AUD $15\,000 stipend per fellow. No application fee.\
 nDuration: 12 months.\n\nMore: https://www.wheelercentre.com/the-next-chap
 ter?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.wheelercentre.com/the-next-chapter?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Melbourne\, Australia\; includes residency at Varuna\, The Nationa
 l Writers' House\, and an end-of-year publishing intensive at The Wheeler 
 Centre.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:adk-ems-berlin-stockholm-residency-2026-27@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: AdK / EMS Berlin-Stockholm Bilateral Residency Program 20
 26-27
DESCRIPTION:A new bilateral residency collaboration between the Studio für
  Elektroakustische Musik at the Akademie der Künste in Berlin and Elektro
 nmusikstudion EMS in Stockholm. Four artists will be selected to develop a
 nd present new works in both cities\, with presentations at KONTAKTE 2027 
 in Berlin and at a corresponding event in Stockholm. The program supports 
 new artistic and technical initiatives at the intersection of sound\, musi
 c\, and technology in the field of time-based\, performative\, and digital
  arts. ELIGIBLE CATEGORIES: (1) new instrumental and live-electronic works
 \; (2) acousmatic music\, computer music\, radio art\, and other forms of 
 electroacoustic music and sound art\; (3) projects from artists of any dis
 cipline for whom sound is a central element\; (4) curatorial\, publishing\
 , and educational projects in sound-based art practice\, particularly thos
 e relating in content to the AdK Studio or EMS\; (5) independent research 
 in acoustics\, computer science\, or musicology -- specifically software d
 evelopment\, spatialization\, or network technologies. Open to individuals
  and groups. Project duration is flexible and arranged by agreement. SUPPO
 RT: travel and accommodation costs for Berlin and Stockholm covered\; pres
 entation fees paid for both venues. Selection is made by the director and 
 advisory board of the Studio für Elektroakustische Musik and the director
  of EMS\; decision is final with no legal entitlement to funding. Incomple
 te or late applications are not considered. This call supplements the Stud
 io's regular residency program (separate deadline June 30\, 2026 for July-
 December 2026 period). Apply exclusively via the online form at https://nc
 .adk.de/index.php/apps/forms/s/HD2nxbzqwgeMHWN6xHg9bQrA. Questions: estudi
 o@adk.de. Deadline: 31 July 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Studio für Elektroakus
 tische Musik\, Akademie der Künste (Berlin) and Elektronmusikstudion EMS 
 (Stockholm)\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany and Stockholm\, Sweden\; travel an
 d accommodation covered for stays in both cities.\nAward: Travel and accom
 modation costs for stays in Berlin and Stockholm covered\; fees paid for p
 resentation at KONTAKTE Festival 2027 (Berlin) and for presentation in Sto
 ckholm. Amount not publicly stated. No application fee.\nDuration: Flexibl
 e\, by agreement\; works to be presented at KONTAKTE 2027 in Berlin and at
  a Stockholm presentation.\n\nMore: https://nc.adk.de/index.php/apps/forms
 /s/HD2nxbzqwgeMHWN6xHg9bQrA?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
URL:https://nc.adk.de/index.php/apps/forms/s/HD2nxbzqwgeMHWN6xHg9bQrA?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany and Stockholm\, Sweden\; travel and accommodation
  covered for stays in both cities.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kb-researcher-in-residence-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260927
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260928
SUMMARY:Deadline: KB Researcher-in-Residence (RiR) 2027
DESCRIPTION:ELIGIBILITY: two Researcher-in-Residence positions in 2027. Ope
 n to early-career researchers of any discipline (data science\, social sci
 ence\, computer science\, humanities) who are currently working on a PhD o
 r within 5 years of their PhD end date. You must have\, or be able to secu
 re\, an affiliation with a Dutch university or research institute willing 
 to second you\; external PhD students may use the funding to obtain such a
  contract. Your project must make use of one or more of the KB digital col
 lections and you must be able to work with primarily Dutch data. You must 
 be available at 0.5 FTE over 6 months and able to spend two days a week on
 -site at the KB in The Hague. COLLECTIONS: over 130 million digitized page
 s of newspapers\, magazines\, radio bulletins and books from 1470 onward (
 via Delpher and DBNL)\, a born-digital web collection of more than 23\,000
  websites\, ground-truth and derived datasets on the KB Lab\, and metadata
  including Linked Data. APPLY: use the official proposal template and subm
 it a single PDF by 27 September 2026 to dh@kb.nl\, after reading the call'
 s terms and conditions\; questions to dh@kb.nl. TIMELINE: deadline 27 Sept
 ember 2026\; internal eligibility review followed by an external committee
  review\; outcome notified November 2026\; residencies start Q1 and Q3 202
 7. DISCIPLINES: digital humanities / data science / computational research
  with cultural-heritage collections. NOTE: the output is usually a dataset
  or tool prototype hosted on the KB Lab\; you agree to share results via b
 log posts on the KB Lab and to publish resulting tools or data under an op
 en license within 6 months of the residency. Proposals should align with t
 he KB Research Agenda or the Cultural AI Lab.\n\nOrganisation: KB\, Nation
 al Library of the Netherlands\nLocation: The Hague\, Netherlands (two days
  per week on-site at the KB premises)\nAward: Secondment at 0.5 FTE for 6 
 months based on your current salary\, up to EUR 5\,590 gross per month for
  a full-time-equivalent position\, plus travel expenses\, office facilitie
 s\, and support from a research software engineer\, research advisor\, and
  collection and data specialists. No application fee.\nDuration: 6 months 
 at 0.5 FTE (two days per week on-site)\; two positions in 2027\, starting 
 Q1 and Q3\n\nMore: https://lab.kb.nl/news/call-kb-researcher-residence-rir
 -2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://lab.kb.nl/news/call-kb-researcher-residence-rir-2027?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands (two days per week on-site at the KB premi
 ses)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ucross-general-residency-spring-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123139Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260715
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260716
SUMMARY:Deadline: Ucross General Residency (All Disciplines): Spring 2027
DESCRIPTION:Ucross offers fully funded artist residencies on a working catt
 le ranch in the foothills of Wyoming's Bighorn Mountains\, providing unint
 errupted time and space free from the pressures and distractions of daily 
 life. Founded in 1981 with its first residency period in 1983\, Ucross hos
 ts approximately 115 individuals per year. Residencies range from two to s
 ix weeks\; at any one time up to ten people are in residence\, typically f
 our writers\, four visual artists\, and two composers. Each artist receive
 s living accommodations\, meals\, and work space at no charge. Lunches and
  dinners are prepared Monday to Friday by a professional chef (lunches del
 ivered to studios\, group dinners at 6 p.m.)\, with ample provisions for b
 reakfasts and weekends\; towels\, linens\, and weekly housekeeping are pro
 vided\, and there is cell service and wireless internet throughout. Reside
 nts provide their own working materials and arrange their own travel to Sh
 eridan\, Wyoming. The program is open to visual artists\, writers\, compos
 ers\, choreographers\, interdisciplinary artists\, performance artists\, a
 nd collaborative teams\; applicants must exhibit professional standing in 
 their field\, and both established and emerging artists are encouraged to 
 apply. Applications are submitted by discipline category: dance\, music/so
 und\, performance\, film/video\, playwriting/screenwriting\, visual art\, 
 fiction\, nonfiction\, poetry\, or interdisciplinary. The work sample and 
 project proposal are the most significant features of the application and 
 should correspond to one another\; if your work is in a single discipline\
 , select the category that best fits your project\, and apply under interd
 isciplinary only if the project genuinely combines multiple disciplines. W
 ork-sample requirements by category: DANCE\, 2-3 video files (each up to 8
  minutes and 200 MB\, or up to 3 Vimeo links\, with a timestamp if longer 
 than 8 minutes)\; MUSIC/SOUND\, 3-5 audio files (each up to 8 minutes and 
 200 MB\, or up to 3 Vimeo links\; musical scores welcome)\; PERFORMANCE an
 d FILM/VIDEO\, 1-3 video files (each up to 5 minutes and under 200 MB\, or
  up to 3 Vimeo/YouTube links\, with a timestamp if longer than 5 minutes)\
 ; PLAYWRITING/SCREENWRITING\, one complete play double-spaced noting the 2
 0-page section to read\; VISUAL ART\, 10 images at 4x6 inches and 300 dpi 
 (JPG or TIF\, no PDFs) plus a data sheet listing title\, medium\, size\, a
 nd year\; FICTION and NONFICTION\, 20 pages of double-spaced writing\; POE
 TRY\, 6-10 poems (10 maximum) in one PDF\, each poem starting on a new pag
 e\, total not exceeding 15 pages\; INTERDISCIPLINARY\, samples representin
 g the genres you plan to work in\, combining any of the above. All written
  work samples must be in English. There is a USD 40 application fee. The o
 pen call for the Spring 2027 session is open May 1 to July 15\, 2026 (appl
 y by 11:59 p.m. MT on July 15). Dedicated Fellowships for Native American 
 Visual Artists and Writers and a separate Culinary Residency are also offe
 red.\n\nOrganisation: Ucross Foundation\nLocation: Sheridan\, Wyoming\, US
 A\nAward: No charge for the residency\; living accommodations\, meals\, an
 d work space provided. USD 40 application fee.\nDuration: Spring session (
 February through early June 2027)\; residencies range from two to six week
 s\n\nMore: https://www.ucrossfoundation.org/residency-program.html?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.ucrossfoundation.org/residency-program.html?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
